{"id": "tea:vadanyaya:1", "source": "src:vadanyaya", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "In debate, the grounds of defeat are only two: for the proponent, failing to state the elements of the proof; for the opponent, failing to point out a real fault. Any other ground of defeat is not reasonable and is not accepted — against the Nyāya list of twenty-two.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute"], "terms": ["trm:nigrahasthana"], "concepts": ["cpt:debate-ethics-buddhist"], "teachers": ["tch:dharmakirti"], "notes": "Opening verse recalled (asādhanāṅgavacana, adoṣodbhāvana).", "coverage": ["B4", "D"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U41-yogacara-pramana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U41-yogacara-pramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
